# INERT exact-purpose proposal for the separate prepare-a-deposit-key enroll
# step. This file is not read by converge and installs no privilege or key.
# The recorded presence-assured enrollment must bind account, receiver host,
# public key, purpose and exact installation record before sender activation.
# Do not substitute the existing kubeconfig receiver or break-glass key.

# The receiver's root-owned copy and its one sudoers rule are no longer
# proposed here: infra/gcp/install-runner-credential-receiver.sh installs
# both on every boss-gcp converge for the ops-runner role (backlog
# 1e50e66b, R-b), and that script is the one place the copied files and
# the rule (the receiver with NO arguments, under env_reset) are spelled.
# The converge records `runner_credential_receiver installed` when it has.
# Root-owned /etc/boss/sor.env supplies the existing system-of-record address.
# jq, bash, coreutils and curl are explicit runtime dependencies.

# Proposed authorized_keys entry, using ONLY the broker-prepared public key
# named by the completed exact-purpose enrollment. It accepts no client
# command, agent forwarding, network forwarding, PTY or environment override.
# Spelled the way the broker joins it (broker_transport_key.rs
# authorized_keys_line) from broker-prepares-the-runner-deposit-key's
# forced_command, so this proposal is the line the enroll step shows
# (pinned by platform_bundle_prepare_a_deposit_key.rs; item 3dc0b247):
command="exec sudo -n /usr/local/libexec/boss/runner-delivery/infra/gcp/runner-credential-recv.sh",restrict @ENROLLED_PUBLIC_KEY@
